<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>4.3.1: Comparing Function Values</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00881</md:content-id>
    <md:title>4.3.1: Comparing Function Values</md:title>
    <md:uuid>9fdcbb13-a1b3-4f53-a2e2-67867f57f0e8</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section id="sect-00001">
      <para id="para-00001">
          <media alt="a drone flying">
            <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_04_06_02_01.jpg"/>
          </media>
        
    </para>
      <para id="para-00002">Here is a graph that represents function <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>, which gives the height of a drone, in meters, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>t</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> seconds after it leaves the ground.</para>
      <para id="para-00003">
          <media alt="Graph. Horizontal axis, 0 to 8, time, seconds. Vertical axis, height, meters. Starting at 0 comma 0, the graph increases linearly. From 2 to 6, it’s horizontal. Then decreases linearly to 7 comma 0.">
            <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_04_06_02_02.svg"/>
          </media>
        
    </para>
      <section class="check-understanding" id="sect-00002">
        <title>Warm Up Activity</title>
        <exercise id="_19dfec9e-2568-4884-8040-50c90159ae7d" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00001">
            <para id="para-00004">Decide which function value is greater.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00001">
            <para id="para-00005">Correct! <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para>
            <para id="para-00006">Nice try! The correct answer is: <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </section>
      <exercise id="exer-00001">
        <problem id="prob-00002">
          <para id="para-00007">Explain your thinking:</para>
          
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00002">
          <para id="para-00008">Compare your answer: Your answer may vary, but here is a sample. 
      The output value at f(4) is greater than the output value at f(0) because at 4 seconds the drone is 4 meters off the ground while at 0 seconds, the drone is on the ground (0 meters).</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <section class="check-understanding" id="sect-00003">
        <exercise id="_9686b5e5-9081-4c5f-9c48-bc94d43a66a3" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00003">
            <para id="para-00009">Decide which function value is greater.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00003">
            <para id="para-00010">Correct! They are equal.</para>
            <para id="para-00011">Nice try! The correct answer is: They are equal.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </section>
      <exercise id="exer-00002">
        <problem id="prob-00004">
          <para id="para-00012">Explain your thinking:</para>
          
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00004">
          <para id="para-00013">Compare your answer: Your answer may vary, but here is a sample. 
      The output value at f(2) is equal to the output value at f(5) because at both 2 seconds and 5 seconds, the drone is 4 meters off the ground.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <section class="check-understanding" id="sect-00004">
        <exercise id="fed73eb3-63f0-418a-aa1e-14cfa827d1d4" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00005">
            <para id="para-00014">Decide which function value is greater.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00005">
            <para id="para-00015">Correct! <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para>
            <para id="para-00016">Nice try! The correct answer is: <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </section>
      <exercise id="exer-00003">
        <problem id="prob-00006">
          <para id="para-00017">Explain your thinking:</para>
          
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00006">
          <para id="para-00018">Compare your answer: Your answer may vary, but here is a sample.
      The output value at f(3) is greater than the output value at f(7) because at 3 seconds the drone is 4 meters off the ground while at 7 seconds, the drone is on the ground (0 meters).</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <section class="check-understanding" id="sect-00005">
        <exercise id="_9e277471-1208-4272-90cd-87faf11ca143" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00007">
            <para id="para-00019">Decide which function value is greater.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00007">
            <para id="para-00020">Correct! It depends on the value of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>t</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
            <para id="para-00021">Nice try! The correct answer is: It depends on the value of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>t</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </section>
      <exercise id="exer-00004">
        <problem id="prob-00008">
          <para id="para-00022">Explain your thinking:</para>
          
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00008">
          <para id="para-00023">Compare your answer: Your answer may vary, but here are some samples. 
  </para>
          <list id="list-00001">
            <item>It depends on the value of t because during some time periods the values of the function are equal.</item>
            <item>It depends on the value of t because between 0-2 seconds, f(t+1) is greater than f(t) but it is exactly the opposite between 5-7 seconds where f(t) is greater.</item>
            <item>It depends on the value of t because between 0-2 seconds, f(t+1) is greater, between 2-5 seconds the values are equal, and after 5 seconds, f(t) is greater.</item>
          </list>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
    </section>
  </content></document>
